<BaseLayout title="Our Team">
  <h1>Our Team</h1>

  <section>
    <h2>Livv — Relational Analyst & Identity Practitioner</h2>

    <p>
      Livv is a millennial based in Brisbane, Queensland, whose life has been
      shaped by a rare combination of high cognitive ability, late‑identified
      neurodivergence, and complex developmental experiences. Recognised early
      for exceptional analytical intelligence, she later received formal
      diagnoses of ADHD and Level 2 Autism — conditions she had already learned
      to navigate through years of highly effective masking and adaptive
      strategies.
    </p>

    <p>
      Her early environment required rapid emotional development and constant
      attunement to others. As a child, she learned to read people and rooms with
      extraordinary speed and accuracy — a skill that matured into a powerful
      relational capacity. Livv can understand interpersonal dynamics almost
      instantly, anticipate needs, and stabilise complex situations with a level
      of emotional intelligence that rivals far more formally accredited
      practitioners.
    </p>

    <p>
      Alongside neurodivergence, Livv carries a history of trauma across
      multiple life domains. Rather than diminishing her, these experiences have
      shaped a deep commitment to dignity, safety, and structural honesty in her
      work. She brings lived experience, analytical clarity, and a rare ability
      to hold complexity without collapsing into sentimentality or detachment.
    </p>

    <p>
      Livv is a lifelong learner with active studies across psychological,
      medical, and coaching domains. She is currently collaborating with
      policymakers on initiatives aimed at improving access to trauma‑responsive
      services for survivors of dissociative and trauma‑related disorders.
    </p>

    <p>
      Outside of practice, Livv is a voracious reader, poet, songwriter, and
      vocalist — someone who thinks deeply, feels precisely, and brings her whole
      self to the work of identity development.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Si — Founder & Relational Identity Practitioner</h2>

    <p>
      Identity Partners was born from Si’s desire to bring his whole self into a
      professional setting — combining emotional warmth with systems‑level
      thinking, relational depth with analytical clarity, and lived experience
      with structured practice. As a neurodivergent practitioner, Si’s
      orientation is shaped by both cognitive pattern‑recognition and relational
      attunement, giving his work a distinctive blend of logic, humanity, and
      coherence.
    </p>

    <p>
      His background spans VCSE community wellbeing work, crisis line listening,
      identity development practice, and social research. These environments
      shaped a professional stance grounded in containment, clarity, and
      structural honesty. Si’s work is relational in nature and logical in
      content: human, attuned, and warm — but also rigorous, conceptual, and
      systemically informed.
    </p>

    <p>
      He draws from a wide theoretical lineage including attachment theory,
      trauma and embodiment, harm reduction, sociological analysis, digital
      hyperconnectivity, and relational ethics. Not as prescriptive models, but
      as conceptual tools for meeting people navigating identity rupture,
      transition, or misalignment.
    </p>

    <p>
      Si works with people who want depth without clinical framing, direction
      without hierarchy, expertise without impersonality, and warmth without
      boundary collapse. His practice is shaped by lived experience, professional
      grounding, and a commitment to helping people understand themselves and the
      lives they are constructing.
    </p>

    <p>
      Identity Partners is the expression of that commitment — a place where
      identity can be explored, built, and sustained through structured relational
      partnership.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
